      "writtenOn": "2020-07-23T10:11:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The .init_rom object included in the RO image is actually copied into RAM (data RAM) by booter.\nThe firmware size that booter will copy is based on the filed \"Firmware Length (offset 25-28)\" in the the bootloader table (The first 64 bytes in the ec.bin).\nNpcx\u0027s ecst tool fills this field according to \"the size of ec.RO.flat - 64 (header size)\" while building the EC image.\nBut it should be fine for the copy because it happens before the firmware starts to initialize and allocate the content for the data RAM. ",
      "revId": "52c4d9f5f9eeea3ab2d4f45ce62e404a52bd63af",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
